{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `log_radon`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the looped manual likelihood contribution `target += normal_lpdf(log_radon[n] | mu[n], sigma_y)` with a single built-in vectorized sampling statement `log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y)`. The predictor vector `mu` is computed deterministically from context data and already-prior-sampled parameters before this observation statement. This preserves the same normal likelihood density while satisfying SafeStan's requirement that the protected observation be scored exactly once by a built-in distribution with a plain top-level data variable on the left-hand side. No data fields were added or changed.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  int<lower=0> J;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=J> county_idx;
  vector[N] floor_measure;
  vector[N] log_radon;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
  real<lower=0> sigma_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma_beta;
  vector[J] alpha_raw;
  vector[J] beta_raw;
  real mu_alpha;
  real mu_beta;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[J] alpha;
  vector[J] beta;
  // implies: alpha ~ normal(mu_alpha, sigma_alpha);
  alpha = mu_alpha + sigma_alpha * alpha_raw;
  // implies: beta ~ normal(mu_beta, sigma_beta);
  beta = mu_beta + sigma_beta * beta_raw;
}
model {
  vector[N] mu;
  // Prior
  sigma_y ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_beta ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma_alpha ~ normal(0, 1);
  mu_alpha ~ normal(0, 10);
  mu_beta ~ normal(0, 10);
  alpha_raw ~ normal(0, 1);
  beta_raw ~ normal(0, 1);

  // Likelihood
  for (n in 1 : N) {
    mu[n] = alpha[county_idx[n]] + floor_measure[n] * beta[county_idx[n]];
  }
  log_radon ~ normal(mu, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"J":1,"N":4,"county_idx":[1,1,1,1],"floor_measure":[2.8757967375942433,2.179789660278225,3.831900202680709,6.585037115243369],"log_radon":[6.415937560510176,3.4926780916399167,3.6384347530145154,3.9572789050896207]}","protected_variables":["log_radon"]}
